## Why the whole system is non-commercial-only

This project's own code (Fase 0) imports functions directly (via Python
import, never copied/vendored) from two sibling repositories at runtime:

- **BCell-Epitope-Prediction** (`Lvera-code/BCell-Epitope-Prediction`):
  CC BY-NC 4.0 for its own code, itself constrained by several
  non-commercial-only external tools it orchestrates (BepiPred-3.0,
  DiscoTope-3.0, AlgPred2, NetMHCIIpan-4.3, NetMHCpan-4.2, ToxinPred2,
  SignalP-6.0 — see that repo's own LICENSE for the full list). This
  project's Fase 0 reuses several of its functions directly.
- **PTM-Prediction** (`Lvera-code/PTM-Prediction`): CC BY-NC 4.0. This
  project's Fase 0 reuses its UniProt REST client
  (`src/structural/uniprot_localization_client.py`, pure stdlib, no
  external tool dependency of its own) for the secretory-pathway and
  quaternary-structure annotations.

Separately, this project clones **BoltzGen** (`HannesStark/boltzgen`,
MIT license) as an external reference/dependency — gitignored, never
vendored into this repository, installed independently by whoever sets up
this pipeline.

Public REST APIs consulted at runtime (UniProt, RCSB PDB) are used only to
read publicly available annotation data for research purposes, not
redistributed as part of this repository.

None of the above are distributed as part of this repository. This LICENSE
file covers only the code actually committed here.

**This is not formal legal advice.** If you intend to use this pipeline or
its outputs beyond non-commercial research/academic purposes, verify the
current license terms of each dependency above directly.
